mended_optimal_distance_km are all null), so POL-RD-05 cannot be invoked either.\n\nNo traffic advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-02847-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. No party named an advisory identifier, so under POL-RD-13 the absence is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, and the deviation stands at the measured figure. The missing artifact carries no fact and does not lower confidence. The trace itself is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) (max gap 0.0 s, 10 s sampling), so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-10(3) does not apply.\n\nPOL-RD-06: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 210 completed trips in the trailing 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no profile-based uplift is taken and no driver-conduct referral arises. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter was mentioned in the debate; it is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. POL-RD-09: no ERP or toll lines are charged and no airport surcharge appears, so there is no pass-through correction and no billing-integrity referral. No driver compensation arises either: the distance charged (67.2 km) is not less than the trace distance, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb has nothing behind it.\n\nConfidence is 0.95. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact - EV-GPS-02847, EV-TRIP-02847 and EV-FARE-02847 - is at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The monetary effect (83.48) exceeds the execution threshold of 8.00 under POL-GEN-05, so the ruling issues but the amount is held in the human queue for release rather than executed automatically. This is a provisional ruling made without human review and either party may appeal it once under POL-GEN-04."
